        'rescuing a ratio R needs M_ta/M_vir = R^3 -- 12.6, 5.4, 6.4, 6.0, 2.6, 1.7 for the six groups -- against '
        'a measured turnaround-to-virial mass ratio of 1.2 to 2.2 in the caustic ensembles. It accounts for the '
        'two mildest rows and not the four largest, though none of the six is individually significant on its own '
        'error bar. AND THE TWO ENSEMBLES THAT LOOK USABLE ARE CIRCULAR, measured here and not read off: both '
        'define their outer radius at a FIXED OVERDENSITY rather than measuring it, and at rho_bar = 3.5 rho_c the '
        'ratio of that radius to the bound is (Omega_Lambda/1.75)^(1/3) = 0.737, at 5.56 rho_c it is 0.632 -- pure '
        'numbers carrying no datum, identical for every cluster in either sample. No published catalogue carries a '
        'kinematic turnaround radius AND an enclosed mass at it; every candidate fails one side. The direction of '
        'the correction is itself contested: the caustic route puts the turnaround-enclosed mass above the virial '
        'one, the Local Volume flow route puts the mass inside the zero-velocity surface at about six tenths of '
        'it, and settling that comes first because the row arithmetic runs through it. Coma now has a kinematic '
        'turnaround radius, a caustic profile and wide-field lensing on one object, so the single-object version '
        'is reachable; the ENSEMBLE is not, and assembling one is a reanalysis of public redshifts rather than a '
        'new survey. The corpus is not exposed: P3 states the radius as general relativity with Lambda and says it '
        'discriminates no cosmology, and the landed confrontation is the Local Group, where the mass is measured '
        'independently of the radius.'
        'r7013 -- THE TWO EXITS, AND THE SECOND ONE IS A MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN A WAIT. WHAT WOULD DISCHARGE '
        'IT is already stated: an ensemble with masses measured inside the turnaround and the radius still '
        'independent of internal dynamics. OR TERMINATES IF: it is demonstrated that no such ensemble can be '
        'built from data that exists OR IS PLANNED, every route being either definitionally circular as the '
        'two fixed-overdensity samples are, or data-limited as the caustic route is -- IN WHICH CASE THE '
        'TERMINAL STATE IS THAT THE BOUND IS A PARAMETER-FREE PREDICTION AWAITING AN INSTRUMENT, a statement '
        'about the skys current reach and not about this construction. Which turns this row from an '
        'indefinite wait into one bounded measurement: it has already established that no PUBLISHED catalogue '
        'carries both sides, so what is owed is the same check against the instruments actually planned, made '
        'once and then stated. '
        'r7027 -- THE LIVE CLAUSE BLOCK. This register is append-forward, so an amended exit condition '
        'APPENDS and never supersedes, and a reader coming down a row meets the OLDEST clause first with '
        'nothing to tell it from the current one. Measured at r7027, one row carried FIVE terminal clauses '
        'and EIGHT discharge clauses set across five revisions of a single day -- each right when it was '
        'made, only the last live, and the gate reporting the row green throughout because it checked that a '
        'clause was PRESENT where the question is which one is CURRENT. So every open row now carries exactly '
        'one live-clause block naming the revision that set it, check_remainder_chains requires exactly one, '
        'and the clause counts are printed rather than hidden. For this row the live clause is unchanged in '
        'substance and is now stated in one place: WHAT WOULD DISCHARGE IT, an ensemble with masses measured '
        'inside the turnaround rather than at the virial radius and the radius still independent of internal '
        'dynamics; OR TERMINATES IF it is demonstrated that no such ensemble can be built from data that '
        'exists OR IS PLANNED, every route being either definitionally circular as the two fixed-overdensity '
        'samples are or data-limited as the caustic route is -- with the terminal state being that the bound '
        'is a parameter-free prediction awaiting an instrument, a statement about the skys current reach and '
        'not about this construction. Which makes the second exit ONE BOUNDED MEASUREMENT rather than an '
        'indefinite wait: the same catalogue check run against the instruments actually planned, made once '
        'and then stated. '
        'r7207: THE SECOND EXIT IS RUN AND IT CLOSES NEGATIVE -- THE ENSEMBLE IS BEING BUILT, so this is a row waiting '
        'for a sample somebody is building, which is the one thing r7027 said it did not know. r7027 bounded this row '
        'by turning its terminal condition into ONE check, the same catalogue check run against the instruments '
        'actually PLANNED, made once and then stated; that check had sat unrun for ninety revisions while this seat '
        'reported the row as not having moved. IT IS THE SECOND CASE. CHANCES, the Chilean Cluster Galaxy Evolution '
        'Survey on 4MOST, targets about 100 clusters -- fifty at z below 0.07 and fifty across 0.07 to 0.45, plus two '
        'superclusters -- OUT TO 5 r200, which its own authors state corresponds roughly to the TURNAROUND RADIUS, at '
        'about 4,500 redshifts per low-z cluster and 2,500 per evolution cluster, over five years. 4MOST took first '
        'light on 18 October 2025. So the terminal condition, that no such ensemble can be built from data that exists '
        'or is planned, is FALSE and the row does not terminate. AND IT CLEARS BOTH DISQUALIFICATIONS THIS ROW '
        'ESTABLISHED: a caustic radius is kinematic and is not defined at a fixed overdensity, so the definitional '
        'circularity that struck the two fixed-overdensity ensembles does not reach it; and the caustic route was '
        'struck as data-limited rather than definitional, which is the defect a survey of this redshift density at this '
        'radius removes. THE NEAR-TERM INSTRUMENT IS THE COUNTER-EXAMPLE and is recorded so this is not read as any new '
        'survey will do: CATARSIS, on TARSIS at Calar Alto, takes 16 clusters at 500-1000 redshifts each but targets '
        'within 2 x R200,c, short of the turnaround by design. The discriminator is the RADIAL REACH, and only one of '
        'the two planned programmes has it. WHAT IS LEFT IS NOT A WAIT: the live obstruction r7027 named is untouched '
        '-- the DIRECTION of the correction is contested in print, the caustic route putting the turnaround-enclosed '
        'mass above the virial one and the Local Volume flow route putting the mass inside the zero-velocity surface at '
        'about six tenths of it, with the rows arithmetic running through it. That disagreement is between published '
        'analyses, is not data-limited, is available now and is this seats. The r7027 terminal condition is retired as '
        'ANSWERED rather than carried forward and is replaced. The corpus is no more exposed than r6893 found it: the '
        'ensemble was never load-bearing and is not load-bearing now that it is coming. '
        'r7211: THE REMAINDER IS ANSWERED AND THE CONTESTED DIRECTION IS NOT CONTESTED -- the two numbers are two '
        'different quantities. r7207 left this rows live item as the contested direction of the correction and set the '
        'terminal condition on it; 60s r7222, pre-registered with its own prediction recorded WRONG, shows there is no '
        'contest. For any non-negative density the enclosed mass is non-decreasing and the turnaround surface lies '
        'OUTSIDE the virial radius, so the quotient is at least one identically; measured over four profile families '
